<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Shadow strength, from API 28 up.

  Elevation on its own was not enough: the framework's default shadow alphas are
  set for a white material surface, and over a warm cream background at those
  values a 6dp lift is nearly invisible. These deepen both the ambient and the
  spot shadow so the same elevation actually reads.

  Deliberately overriding Theme.RatKingRecon rather than Base.Theme, and
  inheriting from Base rather than restating it. The palette stays defined once,
  in values/themes.xml, and the night variant keeps overriding Base underneath
  this - so this file adds two properties and knows nothing about colour.

  Below API 28 the attributes do not exist and shadows keep the platform
  defaults, which is a slightly flatter screen rather than a broken one.
-->
<resources>
    <style name="Theme.RatKingRecon" parent="Base.Theme.RatKingRecon">
        <item name="android:ambientShadowAlpha">0.18</item>
        <item name="android:spotShadowAlpha">0.38</item>
    </style>
</resources>
